k=20 → k=30) to find more similar candidates.\\nL11: 3. **Diverse Search Fallback**: Added a second-pass diverse gene search when similar gene search doesn\'t yield enough candidates, providing broader coverage.\\nL27: The current absolute score approach treats both extremes equally but doesn\'t effectively use the hit label or gene search to find similar candidates.\\nL33: 2. **Better exploitation**: More aggressive gene search around actual hits should find more promising candidates\\nL37: The modification is low-risk because it builds on the proven absolute score approach while adding better hit utilization and more comprehensive gene search.\\n---"\n}'}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': "Great! I can see from the history that there are successful patterns. Let me read one of the successful candidate's model.py files to understand what works:\n", 'tool_calls': [{'id': 'call_0a7ae82d51b34ebf940cdb0d', 'type': 'function', 'function': {'name': 'read_file', 'arguments': '{"file_path": "/inspire/qb-ilm/project/cq-scientific-cooperation-zone/public/ywang/meta-harness-evolver/project/test/project-bda/hoss-evolution-workspaces/Sanchez21/run-1/candidates/candidate_5/harness/model.py"}'}}]}, {'role': 'tool', 'tool_call_id': 'call_0a7ae82d51b34ebf940cdb0d', 'content': '{\n  "content": "  1| from __future__ import annotations\\n  2| import random\\n  3| import numpy as np\\n  4| from collections import defaultdict\\n  5| \\n  6| def select(candidates, history, batch_size, seed) -> list[int]:\\n  7|     \\"\\"\\"\\n  8|     Selection policy for Project-BDA.\\n  9| \\n 10|     Contract (MUST KEEP EXACTLY):\\n 11|         select(candidates, history, batch_size, seed) -> list[int]\\n 12| \\n 13|     Inputs:\\n 14|     - candidates: list[dict]\\n 15|         - single-gene datasets: each item includes {\\"gene\\": \\"<HGNC>\\"}\\n 16|         - gene-pair datasets: each item includes {\\"gene_a\\": \\"<HGNC>\\", \\"gene_b\\": \\"<HGNC>\\"}\\n 17|         - gene search (optional): when enabled by the runner, you may call:\\n 18|           - import bda_tools\\n 19|           - bda_tools.gene_search(query_gene: str, k: int = 10, diverse: bool = False) -> list[int]\\n 20|     - history: list[dict]\\n 21|         - each item includes at least:\\n 22|           - candidate_index: int\\n 23|           - score: float\\n 24|           - hit: int (0/1) if enabled by runner\\n 25|     - batch_size: int\\n 26|     - seed: int\\n 27| \\n 28|     Output:\\n 29|     - list[int] of NEW candidate indices (no repeats; already-selected may be ignored/replaced by runner).\\n 30|     \\n 31|     Strategy: Thompson Sampling with Gene Cluster Priors\\n 32|     - Uses Thompson Sampling (Bayesian bandit algorithm) for adaptive exploration-exploitation\\n 33|     - Models each candidate with Beta distribution based on hit observations\\n 34|     - Uses gene search to create clusters and share information via Bayesian priors\\n 35|     - Naturally balances exploration vs exploitation based on uncertainty\\n 36|     \\"\\"\\"\\n 37|     rng = random.Random(seed)\\n 38|     np.random.seed(seed)\\n 39|     \\n 40|     # Get already selected indices\\n 41|     selected = set(h[\'candidate_index\'] for h in history)\\n 42|     \\n 43|     # Get all available candidate indices\\n 44|     all_indices = list(range(len(candidates)))\\n 45|     available = [i for i in all_indices if i not in selected]\\n 46|     \\n 47|     if len(available) <= batch_size:\\n 48|         return available\\n 49|     \\n 50|     # If no history, use pure exploration\\n 51|     if len(history) == 0:\\n 52|         return rng.sample(available, batch_size)\\n 53|     \\n 54|     # Check if hit information is available\\n 55|     has_hits = any(\'hit\' in h for h in history)\\n 56|     \\n 57|     if not has_hits:\\n 58|         # Fall back to score-based selection using absolute scores\\n 59|         sorted_history = sorted(history, key=lambda x: abs(x[\'score\']), reverse=True)\\n 60|         top_k 